  "meta": {
    "title": "Who Celebrates New Year First, and Who Is Last? 🎆🌍🕛",
    "description": "The first place on Earth to enter the New Year is Kiribati's Line Islands 🇰🇮, like Kiritimati, in UTC+14, the earliest time zone 🎆 Back in 1994 Kiribati moved its eastern islands across the date line, and in 2000 it was the first country to welcome the new millennium 🥳 The last places are Baker Island and Howland Island 🇺🇸, uninhabited US nature reserves in UTC−12. Between the first and the last New Year there are 26 hours! 🤯",
    "pinnedComment": [
      "First and last New Year are only ~2,000 km apart 🤯🎆",
      "What time do you celebrate New Year? 👇",
      "Which time mystery next? 🗺️"
    ],
